---
title: "Diesel Engines I"
code: "DSL-121"
category: "diesel"
credits: "6"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Studies the basic principles involved in the construction and operation of diesel engines. Examines fuel, air, cooling, and control system of various designs. Emphasizes engine overhaul and repair, including gauging proper measuring instruments and tools for these tasks. Part I of II. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 6 hours. Total 8hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
